        <briefdescription>
<para>Buffers a write that fits, and sends a larger one straight to the descriptor after a flush. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A write that does not fit in the free space flushes the buffer first. It is then buffered when it is smaller than bufferSize, so that large text is not copied on its way to the descriptor.</para>
